<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-DJL half-year net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>RTRS-DJL half-year net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		  (A$ million unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating			 profit 7.87 vs loss 11.46</p>
<p>    Net				   loss 1.17 vs loss 22.74</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			  nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales					0.55 vs 470.79</p>
<p>    Other income			    43.81 vs 37.41</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		    loss 3.67 vs loss 6.58</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items		     nil vs profit 221.39</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  loss 0.6 vs loss 12.84</p>
<p>    Tax				credit  1.22 vs credit 0.81</p>
<p>    Interest				   7.18 vs 39.19</p>
<p>    Depreciation			     0.03 s   8.88</p>
<p>NOTE: DJL Ltd is an investment group and is part of the Adelaide Steamship Co Ltd. The results are reported on a consolidated economic entity basis.</p>
<p>DJL said the abnormal loss reflected provision on the diminution of investments and loans.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
